# scripts/spec_freeze_gate.cx — the spec-freeze gate, remediation register R4.1 (#651/#516; RULED (a)
# BY OWNER 2026-08-09 at the post-exit review — the gate was landed with the remediation wave under
# the register's recommended option and the ruling followed; the recorded-ruling match below closed
# with the ruling).
#
# THE RULE (standing, absolute): no normative-spec change lands in the same commit as implementation
# without an EXPRESS recorded ruling. A ruling is referenced from the commit message with a token of
# the form
#     RULED: <row/letter id>          e.g.  RULED: R3.14   /  RULED: L184
# and must exist in the ledgers/register BEFORE the commit (rulings-before-edits, register R4.2). The
# token is machine-checked TWO ways: it must be present, and at least one of its id fragments must
# appear in a recorded ruling store (ledger/**/*.md — the ledgers/registers; recursive, so an
# archived ledger's rulings stay resolvable) — a token naming NO recorded ruling fails the gate.
# Semantic review of the ruling itself stays with humans/audit.
#
# Path classes (R6.1 — the store is a LOCATION, not a filename prefix):
#   ledger          = ledger/** (process records; neither spec nor impl)
#   normative spec  = spec/** — NO exceptions for new work. The LEGACY spellings
#                     spec/02-working/partition_* / batch_* keep their ledger classification so
#                     pre-move history classifies as it did when written; the tree check in default
#                     mode refuses any file re-entering that namespace, so the legacy carve-out is not
#                     a loophole.
#   implementation  = everything else EXCEPT .claude/**, README*, CHANGELOG*, LICENSE*
# A commit touching BOTH spec and impl with no RULED: token is a violation.
#
# Modes:
#   (default)             scan FREEZE_EPOCH..HEAD (every post-audit commit)
#   --check-commit <sha>  check one commit (used by the gate's own tests)
#   --staged              check the git index (pre-commit hook mode); the acknowledgment there is
#                         CX_RULED=<id> in the env, since the message does not exist yet — the range
#                         gate still enforces the message token afterward.
#
# FREEZE_EPOCH = the adversarial-audit commit that recorded the rule. History before it was
# adjudicated BY that audit; history after it is gated here. SPEC_FREEZE_EPOCH overrides it (the
# selftest's planted history). git runs in the current directory, as it always did.
# CXMACH-1 (owner 2026-10-16, (a)): the cx rewrite of spec_freeze_gate.sh, the same lines and exits.
#   $(TOOL_CX) --allow-read --allow-write --allow-env --allow-subprocess scripts/spec_freeze_gate.cx [MODE]
# Exit: 0 = clean; 1 = a violation; 3 = an infrastructure failure (git or the ledger read failed).

[?lib 'cx-stdlib/io'      as=io]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/env'     as=env]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/bytes'   as=bytes]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/process' as=process]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/re'      as=re]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/strings' as=strings]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time'    as=time]

[?def cat scope=public ($parts) [$strings:join $parts '']]
[?def say scope=public impure ($s) [$env:write-line $s]]
[?def cry scope=public impure ($s) [$io:write-line [$env:stderr] $s]]
[?def has scope=public ($rx $s) [$present [$re:find [$re:compile $rx] $s]]]

# Adjudicated commits: authored on a PARALLEL integration lineage where this gate did not run,
# carrying an express owner ruling recorded OUTSIDE the token spelling (rewriting pushed shared
# history to add the token would be worse than the miss). Each row exists ONLY under owner authority
# and names where the ruling is recorded; the skip is LOUD (no-silent-skip rider, GATE_REGISTER.md).
# Full 40-char shas only.
[?def ADJUDICATED-SHAS scope=public () """
0f82c1d36a8a28bddd92442deffb7d94ad692c02 #520 — the DSN-diagnostic fix; the spec-side touch is ONE mechanical version-literal genericization in a 02-working DESIGN LETTER (required by check-version-consistency), no clause or claim changed; ruled under the owner standing autonomy grant 2026-08-20 and recorded LATE per R5.0 in ledger/rulings_2026_08_21_dsn_diagnostic_late_record.md — Class S. NOTE: adjudication authored by the agent that made the miss; flagged for owner review in the cut package.
c920cd9d18b559183a4bc8ea476e1336eee8ada0 #869 — the ORIEL promotion executing TWO recorded rulings (packaging 2b in ledger/rulings_2026_08_19_787_guide_and_packaging.md; R9.2 in ledger/rulings_2026_08_19_0160_cut_path.md): the spec-side paths are the MOVED demo estate, not spec prose; token omitted from the pushed message — Class S
72a6ea437e01e9be9ab1d7dad43a35622f195752 #865 — wave rulings RW65.1/RW65.2 recorded in ledger/rulings_2026_08_19_865_wave.md BEFORE the work (owner '1a 2a'); the commit message cited the ruling ids but omitted the RULED: token — Class S
550f8a1a272ad2e0217fccdb5f0ec44e7e453154 #727-destination-(a) — owner-directed, recorded in the commit message + issue #727; register row: partition_I5_exit_review_packet.md §9 (exit-4a execution record)
a36244f40b17bc4726c4034685e13499b25f8411 #854+#849 — R6.2 batch (owner 2026-08-18 2a); express ruling R5.1 (register), recorded LATE per R5.0 — Class S, ledger/partition_832_process_audit.md Part 1
ab6a62e56530d2a0f1e8542238f843d114036824 #853 — R6.2 batch; express ruling R5.2 (register), recorded LATE per R5.0 — Class S
d3277277351de784e73ef9c482f56d881019233f #840 — R6.2 batch; express ruling R5.3 (register), recorded LATE per R5.0 — Class S
9a76fb184dcd79c575269eda727b8e27a6923db4 #808+#760+#833 — R6.2 batch; rulings 808-1a/760-1a/833-1a recorded BEFORE the work (exit packet §10); message wrote RULED without the colon — Class S
f62deb82c19060385cc87b4c9f88b49f04aa3e74 #823 — R6.2 batch; owner scope ruling recorded (exit packet: SCOPE IS THE WHOLE ISSUE); no token written — Class S
397cbfff151f21bc52286e34879b13d862962789 #819+#817+#778+#740 — R6.2 batch; #817 rides the batch_796 owner ruling (a file the old glob could not read); #819/#778/#740 unrecorded — Class U/M
c5019ca640a90913223216b6d34e9cc1c5784bf1 #844 — R6.2 batch; owner ruling 2a cited, ruled OUTCOME recorded in xap_grammar_composition.md (a working spec, not a store) — Class U
aef85bebbe2ec518625560ce442115e173ada40f #705 — R6.2 batch; media-type ruling recorded in grammar_lexicon_review.md (outside the old glob); rest is stale-citation cleanup — Class U/M
05e4e5d30ac9cadf2680c232031a2e6b93a0ba2f #837 — R6.2 batch; link-path typos + one stale example, no recorded ruling — Class M
efd780b17b6c5511f6a5d3fd16fee549a4fd614d #777-catch-up — R6.2 batch; illustrative enumeration completed, nothing behavioral; 777-1a covers the lane, arguably not this half — Class M
5a6ae8438b78782faa52f32c550b5ab5f16aaca6 #726-init — R6.2 batch; authoring-process §7 status row riding the feature commit, no recorded ruling — Class M
c6caa75609a7e12f0b7a4b60426032be4488fa62 #726-reference — R6.2 batch; spec pointers repointed at the landed app riding the app commit, no recorded ruling — Class M
c21515cb5766f09c1f48247e4e2c42bb4b5591fd #826-proposal — R6.2 batch; the proposal + its rendered demo, approval later given as R5.4 — Class M
2f55cec8c85ee0ebc8bec527834901903347b331 #1106 — limits.md §2 row recording the codec-parser nesting guard: execution of the ruled LIM-1 guard class (#876), spec made to say what ships; token omitted; recorded LATE per R5.0 in ledger/rulings_2026_08_30_text_format_surface.md TF-6 — Class S. NOTE: adjudication authored by the agent that made the miss; flagged for owner review.
b3fe049c59177ede2dd2bcf7219050981e3cb7d9 #1107 — conversions.md §3.1 entity/attr-normalization rows aligned to the owner-authorized fix (session directive 2026-08-30); the prior row described the defect; token omitted; recorded LATE per R5.0 in ledger/rulings_2026_08_30_text_format_surface.md TF-6 — Class S. NOTE: adjudication authored by the agent that made the miss; flagged for owner review.
cd025ce4aea894f5c901e5bdb6c404e0c772e84b #1230 — the root Scope copied at spawn; owner ruling 1a recorded BEFORE the work in ledger/rulings_2026_09_03_shared_scope_1230.md (Q1, RULED 1a); the commit message cited the ruling but wrote RULED without the colon — Class S. NOTE: adjudication authored by the agent that made the miss; flagged for owner review.
162c664ab25b1e40a55998ca06a136de8c7ccd1e #728/#789 — CK-1..CK-6 (connector = feature) RULED (a) BY OWNER 2026-09-06 ('all a on CK-1..CK-6') and recorded BEFORE the edit map in ledger/rulings_2026_09_06_connector_is_a_feature_728.md (ids 728-CK-1 … 728-CK-6); the commit message wrote RULED without the colon; the 'implementation' half is design/** analysis notes, no code — Class S. Owner review 2026-09-06: accepted (1a).
61ab17e1424275c5ed6866706fe1b2dfe62f3e2f #728 — CK-7..CK-10 (client_credentials, Retry-After, pagination, per-feature net reach) RULED (a) BY OWNER 2026-09-06 ('all a if long-term best') and recorded BEFORE the edit map in ledger/rulings_2026_09_06_connector_open_items_728.md (ids 728-CK-7 … 728-CK-10); same colon miss; 'implementation' half is design/728 inventory rows — Class S. Owner review 2026-09-06: accepted (1a).
0d1ff544602339bbf71c91ae1f4e5f0a4a271366 #1331/#1332 — the PAUSED WIP commit ('UNVERIFIED, paused for credits'): the session ran out of budget mid-packet and committed to preserve the work, writing no token. Both defects were recorded BEFORE it, by the owner-ruled connector session, in ledger/rulings_2026_09_06_connector_open_items_728.md ('Two shipped defects found, filed' — #1331 retry backoff, #1332 with-caps resource); the finished packet that supersedes it carries 'RULED: 1331, 1332'. The commit is already PUSHED to origin/impl/1331-retry-delay, so the register's own rule applies — rewriting pushed shared history to add the token would be worse than the miss — Class S. RULED BY OWNER 2026-09-08 (16:25 ET): row RATIFIED — the ruling predates the work, the history is pushed, rewriting it would be worse than the miss; adjudication originally authored by the session that FINISHED the packet and flagged for this review. If the branch is squash-merged this row becomes inert and can be dropped with it.

"""]

[?def is-normative-spec scope=public ($f)
  [?if [or [$strings:starts-with $f 'spec/02-working/partition_'] [$strings:starts-with $f 'spec/02-working/batch_']] [then false] # legacy ledger spelling (pre-R6.1 history only; tree check refuses new files here)
    # the reference-XAP demo ESTATE (#869): versioned implementation living at the spec home — code,
    # instruments, data documents. The freeze gate guards normative PROSE drift; demo maintenance is
    # implementation by definition.
    [else [?if [$strings:starts-with $f 'spec/03-approved/xap/demos/'] [then false]
            [else [$strings:starts-with $f 'spec/']]]]]]
[?def is-impl scope=public ($f)
  [not [or [$strings:starts-with $f 'spec/'] [$strings:starts-with $f 'ledger/'] [$strings:starts-with $f '.claude/']
           [$strings:starts-with $f 'README'] [$strings:starts-with $f 'CHANGELOG'] [$strings:starts-with $f 'LICENSE']]]]
# mixed — true when the paths (one per line) touch BOTH normative spec and implementation.
[?def mixed scope=public ($text)
  [?let [= $ps [?to-sequence [?for [in $p [$strings:split $text "\n"]] [where [not [= $p '']]] [yield $p]]]]
    [and [> [$count [?for [in $p $ps] [where [$is-normative-spec $p]] [yield 1]]] 0]
         [> [$count [?for [in $p $ps] [where [$is-impl $p]] [yield 1]]] 0]]]]

# git — [r ok= rc= out= err=]: one git command in the current directory.
[?def git scope=public impure ($args)
  [?let [= $r [$process:run ('git', [?splice $args]) capture=:both]]
    [?match $r [case [err$e] [r ok=false rc=127 out='' err=[$string $e]]]
      [else [r ok=[= $r@exit-code 0] rc=$r@exit-code out=[$string $r@stdout] err=[$string $r@stderr]]]]]]
# chomp — a command substitution's value: trailing newlines dropped.
[?def chomp scope=public ($s) [$strings:trim-end-chars $s "\n"]]

# strip-unbalanced-parens — a token written parenthesized ("(RULED: 828-1a)") leaves the wrapping ")"
# glued to the last fragment; only UNBALANCED trailing parens are stripped, so a recorded "(…)"
# qualifier inside the id survives intact.
[?def strip-unbalanced-parens scope=public ($f)
  [?loop [= $s $f]
    [?if [not [$strings:ends-with $s ')']] [then [break $s]]
      [else [?if [> [$strings:count $s ')'] [$strings:count $s '(']]
              [then [continue [$strings:slice $s 1 [- [$strings:length $s] 1]]]]
              [else [break $s]]]]]]]

# ledger-text — every ledger/**/*.md file (real files; a symlink is not followed, as grep -r did),
# each read as its bytes; null when the ledger cannot be read (grep's error: rc 2).
[?def ledger-text scope=public impure ()
  [?if [not [$io:is-directory 'ledger/']] [then null]
    [else [?let [= $r [$process:run ('find', 'ledger/', '-type', 'f', '-name', '*.md', '-print0') capture=:both]]
            [?match $r [case [err$e] null]
              [else [?if [not [= $r@exit-code 0]] [then null]
                      [else [$strings:join [?to-sequence [?for [in $p [$strings:split [$string $r@stdout] [$strings:from-code-point 0]]] [where [not [= $p '']]]
                                                [yield [$bytes:to-string-latin1 [?else [$io:read-file-bytes $p] [$bytes:from-string-utf8 '']]]]]]
                                            [$strings:from-code-point 0]]]]]]]]]]
# in-ledger — grep -qrF over ledger/**/*.md: the files are one text joined by NUL, which no fragment
# (a word of a commit message) carries, so a match never spans two files; one search per fragment.
[?def in-ledger scope=public ($texts $frag)
  [$strings:contains $texts [$bytes:to-string-latin1 [$bytes:from-string-utf8 $frag]]]]

# token-recorded — at least one id fragment of any RULED: token payload is found (fixed-string) in the
# ruling stores. Fragments split on + , / and whitespace; each is tried whole and with a trailing (…)
# qualifier stripped, so "R4.4(a-revised)" matches a store that records either spelling. Fragments
# shorter than 2 chars are ignored (never let "a" match everything). [t found= infra=]
[?def token-recorded scope=public impure ($msg $texts)
  [?let [= $frags [?to-sequence
          [?for [in $l [$strings:split $msg "\n"]] [where [$has 'RULED:[[:space:]]*[A-Za-z0-9]' $l]]
                [in $w [?to-sequence [?for [in $x [$re:split [$re:compile "[ \t\n]+"] [$strings:translate [$strings:slice $l [+ [$strings:find $l 'RULED:'] 6] [$strings:length $l]] '+,/' '   ']]] [where [not [= $x '']]] [yield $x]]]]
            [yield [?let [= $a [?let [= $i [$strings:find $w ';']] [?if [$present $i] [then [?if [<= $i 1] [then ''] [else [$strings:slice $w 1 [- $i 1]]]]] [else $w]]]]
                         [= $b [?if [$strings:ends-with $a '.'] [then [$strings:slice $a 1 [- [$strings:length $a] 1]]] [else $a]]]
                     [$strip-unbalanced-parens $b]]]]]]
        [= $wanted [?to-sequence [?for [in $f $frags] [where [>= [$strings:length $f] 2]] [yield $f]]]]
    [?if [= [$count $wanted] 0] [then [t found=false infra=false]]
      [else [?let [= $_t null]
              [?if [= $texts null] [then [t found=false infra=true]]
                # the shell's loop: the first fragment (or its base before the first '(') found in the
                # ledger ends the search.
                [else [t found=[?loop [= $k 1]
                                 [?if [> $k [$count $wanted]] [then [break false]]
                                   [else [?let [= $f [$nth $wanted $k]]
                                     [?if [or [$in-ledger $texts $f]
                                              [?let [= $i [$strings:find $f '(']]
                                                    [= $base [?if [$present $i] [then [?if [<= $i 1] [then ''] [else [$strings:slice $f 1 [- $i 1]]]]] [else $f]]]
                                                [and [not [= $base $f]] [>= [$strings:length $base] 2] [$in-ledger $texts $base]]]]
                                       [then [break true]] [else [continue [+ $k 1]]]]]]]]
                         infra=false]]]]]]]]

[?def INFRA-LEDGER scope=public () 'SPEC-FREEZE-GATE INFRA FAILURE: grep over ledger/ errored (rc 2) — cannot adjudicate; rerun the gate.']

# show-head — `git show --format="  %h %s" --name-only SHA | head -20`, on stderr.
[?def show-head scope=public impure ($sha)
  [?let [= $o [$git ('show', '--format=  %h %s', '--name-only', $sha)]@out]
        [= $ls [$strings:split $o "\n"]]
        [= $n [?if [$strings:ends-with $o "\n"] [then [- [$count $ls] 1]] [else [$count $ls]]]]
        [= $k [?if [> $n 20] [then 20] [else $n]]]
    [?if [= $k 0] [then null] [else [$cry [$strings:join [?to-sequence [?for [in $i [$range 1 $k]] [yield [$nth $ls $i]]]] "\n"]]]]]]

# check-commit — TEXTS is the ledger (ledger-text, null when it cannot be read); 0 clean (or adjudicated), 1 a violation; exits 3 on a ledger read failure and 128
# when the sha does not resolve (git's own message on stderr), as set -e did in --check-commit mode.
# PATHS — the commit's paths when the range's one git log pass already read them (its sha is then
# the full sha git log printed, so neither rev-parse nor git show runs again); null for --check-commit.
[?def check-commit scope=public impure ($sha $strict $texts $paths)
  [?let [= $rp [?if [= $paths null] [then [$git ('rev-parse', $sha)]] [else [r ok=true rc=0 out=$sha err='']]]]
    [?if [not $rp@ok]
      [then [?let [= $_ [?if [= $rp@err ''] [then null] [else [$io:write-string [$env:stderr] $rp@err]]]]
              [?if $strict [then [$env:exit $rp@rc]] [else 1]]]]
      [else [?let [= $full [$chomp $rp@out]]
                  [= $rows [?to-sequence [?for [in $l [$strings:split [$ADJUDICATED-SHAS] "\n"]] [where [$strings:contains $l $full]] [yield $l]]]]
              [?if [> [$count $rows] 0]
                [then [?let [= $row [$strings:join $rows "\n"]] [= $i [$strings:find $row ' ']]
                        [= $_ [$say [$cat ('spec-freeze-gate: ', $sha, ' ADJUDICATED (', [?if [$present $i] [then [$strings:slice $row [+ $i 1] [$strings:length $row]]] [else $row]], ')')]]]
                        0]]
                [else [?if [not [$mixed [?if [= $paths null] [then [$git ('show', '--format=', '--name-only', $sha)]@out] [else $paths]]]] [then 0]
                  [else [?let
                    # A commit message is NEVER empty (the subject line always exists) — an empty read
                    # is a transient infrastructure failure (measured 2026-08-23 under release-verify's
                    # fully parallel `make test`). Retry once; a persistent empty read is ITS OWN loud
                    # failure, never a spec-freeze verdict.
                    [= $m1 [$chomp [$git ('log', '-1', '--format=%B', $sha)]@out]]
                    [= $msg [?if [not [= $m1 '']] [then $m1]
                              [else [?let [= $_s [$process:run ('sleep', '1') capture=:none]] [$chomp [$git ('log', '-1', '--format=%B', $sha)]@out]]]]]
                    [?if [= $msg '']
                      [then [?let [= $_ [$cry [$cat ('SPEC-FREEZE-GATE INFRA FAILURE: git log returned an empty message for ', $sha, ' twice — cannot adjudicate; rerun the gate.')]]] 1]]
                      [else [?if [not [$has 'RULED:[[:space:]]*[A-Za-z0-9]' $msg]]
                        [then [?let [= $_ [$cry [$cat ('SPEC-FREEZE VIOLATION: commit ', $sha, " touches normative spec AND implementation with no 'RULED: <id>' token (register R4.1).")]]]
                                    [= $_h [$show-head $sha]]
                                1]]
                        [else [?let [= $t [$token-recorded $msg $texts]]
                          [?if $t@infra [then [?do [$cry [$INFRA-LEDGER]] [$env:exit 3]]]
                            [else [?if $t@found [then 0]
                              [else [?let [= $_ [$cry [$cat ('SPEC-FREEZE VIOLATION: commit ', $sha, ' carries a RULED: token that names NO recorded ruling in ledger/ (register R4.1 — rulings are recorded BEFORE the work they authorize, R4.2).')]]]
                                          [= $_h [$show-head $sha]]
                                      1]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

# candidates — ONE `git log` pass classifies every commit in the range; check-commit (which classifies
# again, exactly as before) runs only for a commit this pass flags as spec+impl, and for an
# adjudicated row (which it prints). One git show + one rev-parse per commit over ~7,300 commits was
# ~22,000 process spawns: 600-1,500 s of the post-merge run under its own load (cx-private#1917).
# null when git log fails.
[?def candidates scope=public impure ($epoch)
  [?let [= $g [$git ('log', '--no-merges', '--format=%x01%H', '--name-only', [$cat ($epoch, '..HEAD')])]]
        [= $adj [?to-sequence [?for [in $l [$strings:split [$ADJUDICATED-SHAS] "\n"]] [where [> [$count [$strings:split-whitespace $l]] 0]]
                                [yield [$nth [$strings:split-whitespace $l] 1]]]]]
        [= $soh [$strings:from-code-point 1]]
    [?if [not $g@ok] [then null]
      [else [?to-sequence [?for [in $chunk [$strings:split $g@out $soh]] [where [not [= $chunk '']]]
              [yield [?let [= $ls [$strings:split $chunk "\n"]] [= $sha [$nth $ls 1]]
                           [= $paths [$strings:join [?to-sequence [?for [in $i [$range 2 [$count $ls]]] [yield [$nth $ls $i]]]] "\n"]]
                       [?if [or [$mixed $paths] [> [$count [?for [in $a $adj] [where [= $a $sha]] [yield 1]]] 0]] [then [$cat ($sha, "\t", $paths)]] [else '']]]]]]]]]]

[?let [= $av [$env:argv]]
      [= $mode [?if [> [$count $av] 1] [then [$nth $av 2]] [else '']]]
  [?match $mode
    [case '--check-commit'
      [$env:exit [$check-commit [?if [> [$count $av] 2] [then [$nth $av 3]] [else '']] true [$ledger-text] null]]]
    [case '--staged'
      [?if [and [$mixed [$git ('diff', '--cached', '--name-only')]@out] [= [$env:var-or-default 'CX_RULED' ''] '']]
        [then [?do [$cry 'SPEC-FREEZE: the staged change touches normative spec AND implementation.']
                   [$cry 'Either split the commit, or — if an express ruling covers it — set CX_RULED=<row id>']
                   [$cry "and put 'RULED: <row id>' in the commit message (register R4.1/R4.2)."]
                   [$env:exit 1]]]
        [else [$env:exit 0]]]]
    [else [?let
      [= $epoch [$env:var-or-default 'SPEC_FREEZE_EPOCH' 'f964c16a']]
      # R6.1 tree check — the legacy ledger namespace is CLOSED. Ledgers live in ledger/; a file
      # matching the old spelling at HEAD would silently re-enter the historical carve-out above, so
      # its existence is a violation in itself.
      [= $legacy [$sort [?to-sequence [?for [in $p ([?splice [?else [$io:glob 'spec/02-working/partition_*'] ()]], [?splice [?else [$io:glob 'spec/02-working/batch_*'] ()]])] [yield $p]]]]]
      [= $rc0 [?if [= [$count $legacy] 0] [then 0]
                [else [?let [= $_ [$cry 'SPEC-FREEZE VIOLATION: the legacy ledger namespace is closed (R6.1) — these files must live in ledger/:']]
                            [= $_l [$cry [$strings:join [?to-sequence [?for [in $p $legacy] [yield [$cat ('  ', $p)]]]] "\n"]]]
                        1]]]]
      [= $cands [$candidates $epoch]]
      # the ledger is read once for the whole range (the shell grepped it per fragment)
      [= $texts [$ledger-text]]
      [?if [= $cands null]
        [then [?do [$cry [$cat ('SPEC-FREEZE-GATE INFRA FAILURE: git log over ', $epoch, '..HEAD failed — cannot adjudicate; rerun the gate.')]] [$env:exit 3]]]
        [else [?let [= $rcs [?to-sequence [?for [in $s $cands] [where [not [= $s '']]] [yield [?let [= $tab [$strings:find $s "\t"]]
                                                                         [$check-commit [$strings:slice $s 1 [- $tab 1]] false $texts [$strings:slice $s [+ $tab 1] [$strings:length $s]]]]]]]]
                    [= $rc [?if [or [= $rc0 1] [> [$count [?for [in $x $rcs] [where [= $x 1]] [yield 1]]] 0]] [then 1] [else 0]]]
                [?do [?if [= $rc 0] [then [$say [$cat ('spec-freeze-gate: clean (', $epoch, '..HEAD)')]]] [else null]]
                     [$env:exit $rc]]]]]]]]]
